+<body><div class="wrap">
+<div class="kicker">Vocab 0003 · HFT Trading Practice Repo</div>
+<h1>Order-Book Reconstruction from Incremental Feeds</h1>
+<p>Terms introduced by Lesson 0003. Each entry: definition, then a usage sentence as you'd hear it at a desk.</p>
+<div class="scrollbox"><table>
+<tr><th>Term</th><th>Kind</th><th>Definition &amp; usage</th></tr>
+<tr><td class='term'>incremental feed</td><td class='type'>Market data</td><td>A feed that broadcasts every order-level event (add/execute/cancel/delete/replace) and expects each consumer to maintain its own book state, with no resynchronization mechanism.<br><span class='use'>“We consume the ITCH incremental feed, so a single dropped message means our book is wrong until the next session.”</span></td></tr>
+<tr><td class='term'>snapshot feed</td><td class='type'>Market data</td><td>A feed (or endpoint) that periodically publishes the current top-N book levels; consumers hold no state and self-heal on the next snapshot.<br><span class='use'>“The REST snapshot feed is fine for a dashboard, but you can&#x27;t do queue-position research on it.”</span></td></tr>
+<tr><td class='term'>event sourcing</td><td class='type'>Architecture</td><td>Deriving current state exclusively by replaying an ordered log of immutable events — the book is a fold over the message stream.<br><span class='use'>“The order book is event sourcing at nanosecond scale: state equals the fold of every message since the open.”</span></td></tr>
+<tr><td class='term'>phantom depth</td><td class='type'>Failure mode</td><td>Resting size that exists in your reconstructed book but not at the exchange, created by missing or mishandling a removal message.<br><span class='use'>“The crossed top was phantom depth: 18 shares whose X-cancel we skipped in the parser.”</span></td></tr>
+<tr><td class='term'>partial cancel (&#x27;X&#x27;)</td><td class='type'>ITCH message</td><td>ITCH 5.0 Order Cancel: removes a given number of shares from a resting order without deleting it; full removals use &#x27;D&#x27;.<br><span class='use'>“The order died by attrition — three partial cancels and two executions, never a delete.”</span></td></tr>
+<tr><td class='term'>crossed book</td><td class='type'>Market state</td><td>Best bid ≥ best ask. Legitimate transiently pre-open; in continuous trading a persistently crossed reconstruction means stale state, not a real market.<br><span class='use'>“Post-open our book stayed crossed for six hours — a reconstruction bug by definition.”</span></td></tr>
+<tr><td class='term'>stock locate</td><td class='type'>ITCH field</td><td>The per-session integer assigned to each symbol in the Stock Directory (&#x27;R&#x27;); every subsequent message carries it, enabling single-pass symbol filtering.<br><span class='use'>“The filter learns AAPL&#x27;s stock locate from the R message, then keeps everything carrying that locate.”</span></td></tr>
+<tr><td class='term'>market invariant check</td><td class='type'>Testing pattern</td><td>A validation that asserts properties any faithful reconstruction must satisfy on real data (uncrossed post-open book, prices in traded range), catching divergence that unit tests on synthetic input cannot.<br><span class='use'>“Add a market invariant check to the fixture test — spread must be positive after 9:30.”</span></td></tr>
+</table></div>
+</div></body></html>
