+<h1>Kyle&#x27;s Lambda &amp; Price Impact</h1>
+<p>Terms introduced by Lesson 0004. Each entry: definition, then a usage sentence as you'd hear it at a desk.</p>
+<div class="scrollbox"><table>
+<tr><th>Term</th><th>Kind</th><th>Definition &amp; usage</th></tr>
+<tr><td class='term'>Kyle&#x27;s lambda (λ)</td><td class='type'>Statistic</td><td>The OLS slope of price change on signed order flow: dollars of price movement per share of net flow. High λ = shallow/fragile market.<br><span class='use'>“AAPL&#x27;s session λ came out at 1.5e-5 — about 15 cents per 10,000 shares of imbalance.”</span></td></tr>
+<tr><td class='term'>price impact</td><td class='type'>Concept</td><td>The adverse price movement caused by your own trading demand — a cost that grows with size, unlike the fixed per-share spread toll.<br><span class='use'>“The spread is what you pay to trade now; price impact is what you pay to trade big.”</span></td></tr>
+<tr><td class='term'>order-flow imbalance (OFI)</td><td class='type'>Signal</td><td>Cont–Kukanov–Stoikov best-level measure of net buying pressure: depth added to the bid or removed from the ask counts positive, the mirror events negative — quote changes count, not just trades.<br><span class='use'>“OFI went +40 on that event: a buy market order ate 40 shares of the ask.”</span></td></tr>
+<tr><td class='term'>signed volume</td><td class='type'>Signal</td><td>Net traded volume signed by aggressor side; counts only prints, unlike OFI which also counts quote/depth changes.<br><span class='use'>“Signed volume missed the pressure because the asks were pulled, not lifted — OFI caught it.”</span></td></tr>
+<tr><td class='term'>regression observation (bar)</td><td class='type'>Method</td><td>One (x, y) pair fed to OLS — here a 1-second bar: x = summed OFI, y = close-to-close microprice change, so consecutive observations telescope the price path.<br><span class='use'>“23,347 one-second bars went into the session regression.”</span></td></tr>
+<tr><td class='term'>rolling window estimate</td><td class='type'>Method</td><td>Refitting a statistic over consecutive fixed-width time windows to expose intraday variation a single session number would average away.<br><span class='use'>“The rolling window plot shows impact tripling into the close.”</span></td></tr>
+<tr><td class='term'>ok flag / low-confidence gate</td><td class='type'>Design pattern</td><td>Reporting a fitted value together with an explicit trust flag (n_obs ≥ threshold and finite), so under-populated fits are visible but never silently consumed.<br><span class='use'>“That spike window is ok=False — four observations, grey bar, ignore it.”</span></td></tr>
+<tr><td class='term'>r-squared (r²)</td><td class='type'>Statistic</td><td>Fraction of the dependent variable&#x27;s variance the regression explains; says how much of the price move flow accounts for, while λ says how hard flow moves price.<br><span class='use'>“λ tells you the toll; r² tells you how much of the traffic the tollbooth actually sees.”</span></td></tr>
+</table></div>
